  '- For invoice email sending, use send_invoice_email rather than changing invoice status. For draft emails, pass action="draft". To replace generated PDFs on an existing draft without creating another thread or changing its recipients, subject, body, or channel, pass action="draft" plus replace_draft_message_id and omit to, cc, subject, body, scheduled_at, and channel_id; this never sends the email. To send an existing Sanka invoice-email draft, pass action="send" and send_draft_message_id; omit recipient, subject, body, template, attachment, and channel fields so the saved sender/channel, thread, message fields, and attachments are preserved. To schedule an existing draft in place, pass action="schedule", scheduled_at, and schedule_draft_message_id; omit recipient, subject, body, template, attachment, and channel fields. Confirm the returned from_email, reply_to_email, provider, and history_locations. A saved Gmail/SMTP channel is preserved; a draft without a channel uses the managed invoice sender. For new scheduled sends, pass action="schedule" and scheduled_at as an ISO datetime in the user/workspace timezone. To attach generated PDFs such as an invoice plus delivery note, pass additional_pdf_attachments with template_select, object_type, record_id, and filename as needed.',
